.TH SIMULATE-PREGAME-BATCH 1 "November 2026" "Legendary Picks" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
simulate-pregame-batch \- run reproducible NFL full-game simulations
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B python3 scripts/nfl_sequence/simulate_pregame_batch.py
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs a batch of NFL game simulations from a frozen pregame snapshot and pinned model inputs. The output reports score
and win distributions and retains a result for each requested seed. Forecast score distributions use valid, untied,
complete games. The output also records invalid and incomplete seeds and their reasons.
.PP
Supply either a published schedule game and a timezone-qualified cutoff, or a hash-pinned snapshot file. A normal
SLC-v2 run also needs its season snap-count input and SHA-256. The
.B --slc-v2
flag enables the SLC-v2 model layers; it does not select an older SLC version.
.PP
Box-score sidecars and ordered play rows are both enabled by default. Play rows are stored in the box-score sidecar,
with before/after game state and play outcomes. This can use substantial disk space for large runs. Use the explicit
.B --no-export-plays
option to omit ordered plays. Use
.B --no-export-boxscores
with
.B --no-export-plays
to omit both outputs.
.PP
Resume reuses saved seeds. It refuses to rerun a completed seed when the saved result lacks an export requested by the
current command. Disable the missing export or choose a new output path to run a new simulation.
.SH OUTPUTS
.TP
.B --out FILE
Required. Main batch JSON output. The seed ledger is stored beside it with the ".seeds.jsonl" suffix. The default
box-score sidecar uses the ".boxscores.jsonl" suffix.
.TP
.B Box-score sidecar
One versioned per-seed box score per game, plus a manifest row. By default, each game row also contains a realism block
with ordered play rows and the lineup summary when the participation model ran.
.TP
.B Seed ledger
One row per seed, including status, result, and player totals. A resume must use the same pinned input identities.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show all command-line options and exit.
.SS Game and snapshot inputs
.TP
.BI \-\-game-id " ID"
Published nfl_schedule game ID. Required unless --snapshot-file is used.
.TP
.BI \-\-as-of " TIME"
Timezone-qualified ISO-8601 information cutoff. Required unless --snapshot-file is used.
.TP
.BI \-\-kickoff-utc " TIME"
Explicit kickoff time in UTC when schedule data does not provide the needed value.
.TP
.BI \-\-kickoff-source-url " URL"
Source URL supporting an explicit kickoff time.
.TP
.B --allow-unverified-current-schedule-exploratory
Allow use of the current schedule row when a cutoff-versioned row is unavailable. The run is marked exploratory and
retains the row's actual ingestion time.
.TP
.BI \-\-snapshot-file " FILE"
Hash-pinned pregame snapshot JSON, or a game payload containing one. Replaces schedule lookup inputs.
.TP
.BI \-\-db " FILE"
SQLite database path. Opened read-only. Default: the simulator's configured NFL database.
.TP
.BI \-\-roster-snapshot " FILE"
Optional pinned full-depth roster JSON with starter flags and jersey numbers.
.TP
.BI \-\-roster-provenance " FILE"
Source and checksum manifest for --roster-snapshot.
.TP
.BI \-\-availability-store " DIR"
Use the newest availability snapshot frozen by --as-of. Requires --roster-snapshot.
.TP
.BI \-\-availability-snapshot " FILE"
Use this availability snapshot instead of selecting one from --availability-store. Requires --roster-snapshot and
roster provenance.
.TP
.BI \-\-news-evidence-dir " DIR"
Read captured RotoWire evidence bound to the frozen snapshot. Evidence does not change roster, availability, or workload
inputs. Incompatible with --availability-store and --availability-snapshot.
.TP
.BI \-\-game-info-snapshot " FILE"
Attach frozen venue, kickoff, forecast, referee, and broadcast context. The model does not read this context.
.SS Model and research configuration
.TP
.BI \-\-slc-profile " PROFILE"
Named layer configuration: custom, s0, or v1_full_stack. Default: custom. Custom preserves manual feature flags.
.TP
.B --slc-v2
Enable the SLC-v2 configuration on v1_full_stack, including V1.5 season adaptation, V2 layers, and RNG protocol v2.
Requires --participation-snap-counts and its SHA-256. Explicit input tables replace pinned defaults.
.TP
.BI \-\-slc-disable-layer " NAME"
Disable one optional SLC layer. Repeat to disable multiple layers.
.TP
.BI \-\-playcall-artifact " FILE"
Frozen SLC play-call artifact. Its source pool is restricted to seasons before the game season.
.TP
.B --playcall-season-adapt
Blend cutoff-safe current-season team outcomes into team splits. Requires --playcall-team-outcomes.
.TP
.BI \-\-season-adapt-n0 " N"
Historical prior weight for season adaptation. Default: 4.
.TP
.B --playcall-team-outcomes
Reweight sampled outcome classes using team offense and defense splits within the selected play-call intent.
.TP
.B --playcall-point-splits
Use prior-season team score-state shifts to adjust dropback rate.
.TP
.BI \-\-playcall-point-splits-cache " FILE"
Use this frame cache for point splits instead of rebuilding it from the database.
.TP
.B --playcall-streak-splits
Use prior-season team win/loss streak splits. Requires --playcall-streak-file.
.TP
.B --playcall-streak-league
Use league-wide streak splits for dropback rate and outcome mix.
.TP
.BI \-\-playcall-streak-file " FILE"
Verified team win/loss streak records in the wl-streaks JSON format.
.TP
.BI \-\-playcall-streak-cache " FILE"
Frame cache for streak splits.
.TP
.B --playcall-target-roles
Use team-by-situation target-role priors before selecting the play outcome.
.TP
.B --playcall-playbook
Use team playbook priors for pass depth, pass location, and run gap. Requires --playcall-decision.
.TP
.B --playcall-dirichlet-shares
Use prior-season per-game Dirichlet player target and carry shares. Implies --playcall-player-shares.
.TP
.B --playcall-player-shares
Draw pre-event receivers and carriers using prior-season player shares.
.TP
.B --playcall-player-outcomes
Condition QB, receiver, and rusher outcomes on the selected player.
.TP
.B --playcall-player-outcomes-receiver-only
Condition player outcome draws on the receiver only. Requires --playcall-player-outcomes.
.TP
.B --playcall-qb-decisions
Use QB-specific target-role and scramble decisions from prior seasons.
.TP
.B --playcall-qb-run-role-style
Adjust QB run-role selection using the named QB's prior non-scramble run tendency. Requires --playcall-qb-decisions.
.TP
.B --playcall-decision
Use decision categories A through N as pre-event draws and condition outcomes on them.
.TP
.B --playcall-decision-unfiltered
With --playcall-decision, apply outcome lifts but draw the row from the whole situation cell.
.TP
.B --playcall-coverage
Condition dropback outcomes on prior-season defensive coverage shares.
.TP
.B --playcall-formation
Use prior-season formation and personnel and condition outcomes on them. Requires --playcall-artifact.
.TP
.B --playcall-exact-yardline
Inside the 20, draw outcomes from source plays at the exact yard line.
.TP
.B --playcall-pbv1-package FILE
Use the PBV1 RB-only package sampler for personnel labels. Off by default.
.TP
.BI \-\-participation-field " FILE"
Use the skill-position lineup transition model. Requires its SHA-256 and RNG protocol v2. Incompatible with
--playcall-pbv1-package.
.TP
.BI \-\-participation-field-sha256 " SHA256"
Expected SHA-256 of --participation-field.
.TP
.BI \-\-participation-snap-counts " FILE"
Cutoff-safe current-season snap-count update for the lineup table. Requires --participation-field and its own SHA-256.
.TP
.BI \-\-participation-snap-counts-sha256 " SHA256"
Expected SHA-256 of --participation-snap-counts.
.TP
.BI \-\-playcall-fg-kicker " FILE"
Kicker-specific field-goal model table. Requires its SHA-256, --playcall-artifact, and the
long_field_goal_feasibility blocker fix.
.TP
.BI \-\-playcall-fg-kicker-sha256 " SHA256"
Expected SHA-256 of --playcall-fg-kicker.
.TP
.B --experimental-workload-estimator {C,D1}
Select the historical-share C control or adaptive-share D1 workload estimator. D1 is the preferred research estimator.
.TP
.BI \-\-workload-adaptive-input " FILE"
Frozen workload adaptation input for D1.
.TP
.BI \-\-workload-adaptive-sha256 " SHA256"
Expected SHA-256 for --workload-adaptive-input. Required with that input.
.TP
.BI \-\-workload-concentrations " FILE"
Experimental fitted workload concentrations.
.SS Simulation size, seeds, and execution
.TP
.BI \-\-games " N"
Number of seeds to run. Default: 10000.
.TP
.BI \-\-seed-start " N"
First seed ID for a contiguous run. Default: 1.
.TP
.BI \-\-seed-list-file " FILE"
JSON object with a seeds array. Runs exactly those unique, non-negative seed IDs.
.TP
.B --resume
Resume the seed ledger beside --out. Refuses changed input identities and refuses to rerun completed seeds whose saved
records lack requested box-score or play exports.
.TP
.BI \-\-progress-every " N"
Print progress every N games. Default: 1000. Set to 0 to disable.
.TP
.BI \-\-max-simulation-errors " N"
Stop once errors exceed N. Default: 0, which stops on the first simulation error. Finished seeds remain in the ledger.
.TP
.BI \-\-rng-protocol " {v1,v2}"
Random stream protocol. SLC uses v2 by default; without SLC the default is v1. Explicit v1 replays legacy draws.
.TP
.B --paired-randomness
Isolate random draws by game snapshot, drive, play, and semantic event for matched-seed experiments.
.TP
.BI \-\-expected-stream-root-sha256 " SHA256"
Require this baseline v2 stream root before running seeds. Required for sack ablation.
.SS Blocker and scoring controls
.TP
.BI \-\-slc-blocker-fix " FIX"
Enable one blocker fix; repeat to select several. Choices: run_scramble_backoff, long_field_goal_feasibility,
blocked_kick_source_audit, blocked_kick_geometry, safety_free_kick_boundaries. With a play-call artifact, all are on by
default. Use --no-slc-blocker-fixes to disable them.
.TP
.B --no-slc-blocker-fixes
Disable ordinary blocker fixes.
.TP
.BI \-\-slc-fg-ordinary-cutoff " YARDS"
Maximum ordinary field-goal decision distance when long_field_goal_feasibility is enabled. Default: 60.
.TP
.B --ablation-restore-sack-mass
Paired ablation that substitutes sacks for incomplete passes at the observed cell rate. Requires RNG v2 and
--expected-stream-root-sha256.
.TP
.B --try-policy {unconditional,k1}
Try-policy setting. Default: unconditional.
.TP
.B --no-safety-table
Disable observed safety free kicks and retain the old safety blocker.
.SS Historical and context controls
.TP
.B --historical-archive-reconstruction
Admit pinned historical inputs as retrospective. Does not relax prospective capture checks.
.TP
.BI \-\-readiness-matrix " FILE"
Per-game readiness matrix required for historical archive reconstruction.
.TP
.BI \-\-archive-manifest " FILE"
Dated source release hashes and publication times required for historical reconstruction.
.TP
.BI \-\-archive-root " DIR"
Archived source files. Each is rehashed against both archive manifests.
.TP
.BI \-\-historical-streak-file " FILE"
Optional explicit path for the archive-reconstructed pregame streak file.
.TP
.B --context-mode {unconditioned,cutoff_unconditioned,offense,defense,both}
Contextual source-pool mode. Default: unconditioned. Offense/defense modes are research ablations.
.TP
.BI \-\-context-bandwidth " N"
Gaussian kernel bandwidth in source team-rating standard deviations. Default: 1.
.TP
.BI \-\-context-min-source-games " N"
Minimum effective source games for a sampled contextual pool cell. Default: 10.
.TP
.B --team-tendency
Drive policy from prior-season team tendencies. Requires --context-mode cutoff_unconditioned.
.TP
.BI \-\-home-market-margin " POINTS"
Optional expected-margin line for the home team. Positive means the home team is favored.
.TP
.BI \-\-market-total " POINTS"
Optional over/under total line.
.SS Output and run registration
.TP
.BI \-\-out " FILE"
Required output JSON path.
.TP
.B --export-boxscores
Write per-seed box-score sidecar and valid-game distributions. Default: on.
.TP
.B --no-export-boxscores
Disable the box-score sidecar. Also requires --no-export-plays.
.TP
.B --export-plays
Include ordered realized play rows, before/after states, outcomes, and lineup summary in each box-score row. Default: on.
.TP
.B --no-export-plays
Omit ordered play rows from box-score rows.
.TP
.BI \-\-register-dir " DIR"
Register the run read-only in this store and append its index line.
.TP
.BI \-\-paired-layer-baseline-ledger " FILE"
Verified v2 control ledger for one disabled-layer paired ablation.
.TP
.BI \-\-paired-workload-baseline-ledger " FILE"
Control ledger for a paired workload-only experiment.
.TP
.BI \-\-paired-lineup-baseline-ledger " FILE"
Control ledger for a paired snap-count lineup experiment.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run 10,000 SLC-v2 seeds from a frozen game snapshot and retain box scores with all play rows:
.PP
.nf
python3 scripts/nfl_sequence/simulate_pregame_batch.py \
  --snapshot-file game-snapshot.json \
  --playcall-artifact playcall-model.json \
  --slc-profile v1_full_stack --slc-v2 \
  --participation-snap-counts snap-counts.json \
  --participation-snap-counts-sha256 SHA256 \
  --games 10000 --seed-start 1 --out tonight.json
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR simulate_pregame_batch.py --help
